## 🎯 Quick Checklist Before Launch

1. ✅ All core pages built and wired up  
2. ✅ Responsive design passes mobile & desktop tests  
3. ✅ Accessibility audit (WCAG 2.1 AA) passes  
4. ✅ SEO audit (meta tags, structured data) passes  
5. ✅ Unit + E2E tests all green  
6. ✅ Performance score > 90 (Lighthouse)  
7. ✅ Security hardening (CSP, XSS protection)  
8. ✅ Analytics & error monitoring (Sentry, Plausible) set up  
9. ✅ CI/CD pipeline running on every push  
10. 🚀 Deploy to production

---

### Final Thought

Building a robust e‑commerce frontend is a marathon, not a sprint. Start small—get a minimal viable product (MVP) up and running, then iterate. Keep the code modular, test-driven, and well‑documented. With the stack above, you’ll have a solid foundation that scales, performs, and delights both users and stakeholders. Happy coding!
